      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Two general merchandise stores, Callicott and Brashears, and a lumber yard and flour mill defined Portland’s bustling business scene by 1900.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        23,
        24
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.callawaymohistory.org/portland/",
      "category": "economy",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Portland sits between bluffs along the Missouri River, where Native American burial mounds and fur trapper artifacts have been found.",
